40573423,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,Yes,"The study included 487 PWH (People With HIV): 99 from 2021, 143 from 2022, 148 from 2023, and 97 from 2024. The genotypes of 487 PWH diagnosed from 2021 to 2024 were analyzed, and sequences were generated for the analysis of drug resistance.","The paper mentions the analysis of genotypes from 487 PWH diagnosed from 2021 to 2024, indicating that HIV sequences were obtained from patient samples."
40573423,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,Yes,"Drug resistance analysis included 417 PWH from 2021 to 2024. The average drug resistance across classes was 1.9%, 4.1%, 4.9%, and 3.3% in 2021, 2022, 2023, and 2024, respectively. Although a slight increasing pattern was observed in the prevalence from 2021 to 2024, it showed no statistically significant pattern (p = 0.495). The most frequent single-class mutations were against NNRTIs (18/284, 6.3%), followed by INSTIs (14/364, 3.8%), NRTIs (9/284, 3.2%), and PIs (5/281, 1.8%).","The paper mentions that drug resistance was analyzed for 417 patients, including all currently available drugs. The data are presented in tables and figures, indicating in vitro susceptibilities to known drugs."
40573423,3,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,Not Reported,No relevant evidence found in the provided text.,The paper does not provide specific GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates.
40573423,4,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,"pol, gag, env","Reverse transcription and nested PCR were performed to amplify the envelope (env), gag protein (gag), and pol protein (pol) for genotyping and the protease, reverse transcriptase, and integrase genes for drug resistance analysis.","The paper mentions that the envelope (env), gag protein (gag), and pol protein (pol) were amplified for genotyping and drug resistance analysis, indicating these genes were sequenced."
40573423,5,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,South Korea and unspecified countries in Asia and the Americas,"Demographic data were obtained from the Division of HIV/AIDS Prevention and Control at the KDCA. Recently diagnosed PWH who had not been exposed to ART were included. The initial diagnosis for all included PWH was made between January 2021 and October 2024. Within the broader context of HIV-1 epidemiology in Asia and the Pacific, the findings contribute to a comprehensive understanding of the global distribution of HIV-1 resistance and genotypes, enabling the development of effective interventions. All positive specimens nationwide are sent to the KDCA for surveillance to monitor recent HIV infection [15]. Table 2. Demographics of study population (2021-2024).",The paper specifies that the study was conducted in South Korea and mentions that non-Korean participants primarily came from Asia and the Americas.
40573423,6,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,2021 to 2024,"The study included 487 PWH: 99 from 2021, 143 from 2022, 148 from 2023, and 97 from 2024. In South Korea, HIV confirmatory testing is conducted by the Korea Disease Control and Prevention Agency (KDCA) and 17 provincial Institutes of Health and Environment. All positive specimens nationwide are sent to the KDCA for surveillance to monitor recent HIV infection. Recently diagnosed PWH who had not been exposed to ART were included. The initial diagnosis for all included PWH was made between January 2021 and October 2024.",The paper mentions that the samples were obtained from individuals diagnosed between January 2021 and October 2024.
40573423,7,What method was used for sequencing?,Sanger sequencing,Sanger sequencing was performed using in-house sequencing primers (Table 1).,The paper states that Sanger sequencing was performed using in-house sequencing primers.
