40596906,14,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"NRTIs, NNRTIs","Among the NRTI resistance-associated mutations, M184V was the most frequent (26.7%). Mutations conferring resistance to efavirenz, nevirapine, lamivudine, abacavir, and didanosine were frequently observed in children and mothers. Except for three mother-child pairs that did not exhibit antiretroviral resistance mutations, all pairs showed the presence of mutations that conferred high-level resistance in at least one member of the pair (Fig. 3).",The paper provides evidence of received NRTI and NNRTI drug classes before genotyping.
40596906,15,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"Zidovudine (ZDV), Lamivudine (3TC), Nevirapine (NVP), Lopinavir/ritonavir, Efavirenz (EFV), Abacavir (ABC), Didanosine (DDI)","Among nine children who had initiated ART, zidovudine (ZDV) + lamivudine (3TC) + nevirapine (NVP) was administered to three (20%), ZDV + 3TC + lopinavir/ritonavir to two (13.3%), and ZDV + 3TC + efavirenz (EFV) to two (6.7%). Pre-treatment genotyping was performed on treatment-naive women, and women living with HIV-1 during prior treatment underwent genotype tests due to virological failure. Antiretroviral drug regimens commonly in use by mothers who were included in this study were those consisting of NRTIs in addition to a protease inhibitor (PI) or a NNRTI: ZDV +3TC + EFV, ZDV +3TC + LPV/r, ZDV +3TC + NVP, ZDV +3TC + abacavir (ABC), ZDV +3TC + rilpivirine (RPV), ZDV +3TC + tenofovir disoproxil fumarate (TDF), and abacavir (ABC) + 3TC + K103N + EFV trap. $12	ext{ 	extdollar }$ were collected in couriers.once.",The paper lists various drugs that were part of the ART regimens received by mothers and children prior to sequencing.
