40974886,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,Yes,"Historical RNA or proviral DNA genotype reports for protease (PR), reverse transcriptase (RT), and integrase (IN) from local laboratories or commercial sites were included.","The paper includes historical RNA and proviral DNA genotype reports, indicating that HIV sequences from patient samples were analyzed."
40974886,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,No,"The study included treatment-experienced PWH aged ≥ 18 years, randomized to B/F/TAF or comparator regimens in studies GS-US-380-4449 (NCT03405935 [5,6]; ≥ 65 years), GS-US-380-4030 (NCT03110380 [7]), and GS-US-380-4580 (NCT03631732 [8]), with virologic suppression (HIV-1 RNA < 50 copies/mL) for ≥ 3-6 months and no prior virologic failure on integrase strand transfer inhibitor (INSTI)-containing regimens (GS-US-380-4030, GS-US-380-4580) or no HIV-1 RNA ≥ 400 copies/mL (GS-US-380-4449). Full resistance criteria for each study are available.","The study design involved genotyping from clinical trials, focusing on resistance-associated mutations (RAMs) rather than in vitro drug susceptibility testing."
40974886,3,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,Not reported,No evidence found,The paper does not mention any GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates.
40974886,4,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,"PR, RT, IN","Historical RNA or proviral DNA genotype reports for protease (PR), reverse transcriptase (RT), and integrase (IN) from local laboratories or commercial sites were included.","The paper reports genotyping of protease, reverse transcriptase, and integrase from the study participants."
40974886,5,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,USA,"Genotypic data were available from 223 and 25 participants for the 2- and multiple-timepoint analyses, respectively (7 participants had IN data at 2 pre-switch timepoints and PR/RT data at ≥3 pre-switch timepoints and were included in both analyses).","The samples were obtained from participants in the USA, as indicated by the study's affiliation with Monogram Biosciences, CA, USA."
40974886,6,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,1997 to 2019,"Genotypic data were available from 223 and 25 participants for the 2- and multiple-timepoint analyses, respectively (7 participants had IN data at 2 pre-switch timepoints and PR/RT data at ≥3 pre-switch timepoints and were included in both analyses). For the 2-timepoint analysis, 430 PR/RT and 140 IN reports were analyzed from 215 and 70 participants, respectively. The majority of IN reports were 1-3 years apart (69%; 48/70), and approximately half (48%; 104/215) of PR/RT reports were ≥5 years apart (Supplemental Table 2). For PR/RT genotypes, most comparisons were RNA to DNA (79%; 169/215) or DNA to DNA (20%; 44/215), with RNA to RNA occurring rarely (1%; 2/215). For IN, most reports compared DNA to DNA (66%; 46/70); the remaining were RNA to DNA (34%; 24/70). For the multiple-timepoint analysis, 98 reports (97 PR/RT and 5 IN) from 25 participants were included. Most reports (88%; 22/25) had ≥5 years between the first and last test (median [Q1, Q3] 9.3 [5.7, 14.4] years) (Supplemental Table 2).",The paper mentions that genotype reports were collected from March 1997 to March 2019.
40974886,7,What method was used for sequencing?,Population sequencing,Genotypic data were reported on a population sequencing level.,The paper states that genotypic data were reported on a population sequencing level.
40974886,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,No,"The study included treatment-experienced PWH aged ≥ 18 years, randomized to B/F/TAF or comparator regimens in studies GS-US-380-4449 (NCT03405935 [5,6]; ≥ 65 years), GS-US-380-4030 (NCT03110380 [7]), and GS-US-380-4580 (NCT03631732 [8]), with virologic suppression (HIV-1 RNA < 50 copies/mL) for ≥ 3-6 months and no prior virologic failure on integrase strand transfer inhibitor (INSTI)-containing regimens (GS-US-380-4030, GS-US-380-4580) or no HIV-1 RNA ≥ 400 copies/mL (GS-US-380-4449). Full resistance criteria for each study are available [5-8]. All studies were undertaken in accordance with the Declaration of Helsinki. The study protocols were approved by independent review boards or ethics committees [5-8]. All participants provided written informed consent for the primary study analyses.",The paper does not mention any cloning of samples prior to sequencing.
40974886,9,What type of samples were sequenced?,Whole blood,"From each whole blood sample, reproducibility (%) of proviral RAM reporting was the number of times the mutation was detected per number of assays run (2-4 replicates).",The paper states that whole blood samples were used for genotyping.
40974886,10,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,No,"The study included treatment-experienced PWH aged − 3–6 months and no prior virologic failure on integrase strand transfer inhibitor (INSTI)-containing regimens (GS-US-380-4030, GS-US-380-4580) or no HIV-1 RNA ≥ 400 copies/mL (GS-US-380-4449). Full resistance criteria for each study are available [5–8].",The study participants had virologic suppression and no prior virologic failure.
40974886,11,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,Yes,"The study included treatment-experienced PWH aged ≥ 18 years, randomized to B/F/TAF or comparator regimens in studies GS-US-380-4449 (NCT03405935 [5,6]; ≥ 65 years), GS-US-380-4030 (NCT03110380 [7]), and GS-US-380-4580 (NCT03631732 [8]).",The participants were enrolled in clinical trials as indicated by the study design.
40974886,12,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,223,"Genotypic data were available from 223 and 25 participants for the 2- and multiple-timepoint analyses, respectively (7 participants had IN data at 2 pre-switch timepoints and PR/RT data at ≥3 pre-switch timepoints and were included in both analyses).",The paper states that genotypic data were available from 223 participants for the 2-timepoint analysis.
40974886,13,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,Yes,"The study included treatment-experienced PWH aged ≥ 18 years, randomized to B/F/TAF or comparator regimens in studies GS-US-380-4449 (NCT03405935 [5,6]; ≥ 65 years), GS-US-380-4030 (NCT03110380 [7]), and GS-US-380-4580 (NCT03631732 [8]).","The study included treatment-experienced people with HIV (PWH), indicating that they had previously received antiretroviral drugs."
40974886,14,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"NRTI, NNRTI, PI, INSTI","The study included treatment-experienced PWH aged ≥ 18 years, randomized to B/F/TAF or comparator regimens in studies GS-US-380-4449 (NCT03405935 [5,6]; ≥ 65 years), GS-US-380-4030 (NCT03110380 [7]), and GS-US-380-4580 (NCT03631732 [8]).","The participants were switched to a B/F/TAF regimen, indicating prior use of NRTI, NNRTI, PI, or INSTI drug classes."
40974886,15,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"Bictegravir, emtricitabine, tenofovir alafenamide","The study included treatment-experienced PWH aged ≥ 18 years, randomized to B/F/TAF or comparator regimens in studies GS-US-380-4449 (NCT03405935 [5,6]; ≥ 65 years), GS-US-380-4030 (NCT03110380 [7]), and GS-US-380-4580 (NCT03631732 [8]).","The study involved participants switched to a regimen containing bictegravir, emtricitabine, and tenofovir alafenamide."
