41004608,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,Yes,"A total of 1182 people had available WGS data between 2015 and 2021. Of these, 76 HIV acquisitions could not be confirmed to be recent. The UKHSA has sequenced HIV whole genomes from all individuals identified to have recently acquired HIV-1 in the UK since 2015 as part of routine HIV surveillance.",The paper mentions that 'the UKHSA has sequenced HIV whole genomes from all individuals identified to have recently acquired HIV-1 in the UK since 2015 as part of routine HIV surveillance.' This indicates that the sequences were obtained from patient samples.
41004608,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,No,"The complete genomic sequencing of HIV was performed using a previously described sequence capture method and the short read data were assembled into consensus whole genomes using Genomancer, an in-house viral genome assembly pipeline. We did not see any significant impact of the nonintegrase mutations considered, either in univariable nor multivariable analysis, on time to virological suppression or viral blip. Though these mutations have been shown to play a role directly, or in facilitating INSTI resistance in vitro, this was not replicated in vivo within our sample",The paper does not mention any in vitro drug susceptibility testing. It focuses on sequencing and analyzing mutations in patient samples rather than performing drug susceptibility assays in vitro.
41004608,3,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,Not reported,No GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates were provided in the text of the paper.,The paper does not provide any GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates. It focuses on the analysis of mutations and their prevalence without mentioning specific accession numbers.
41004608,4,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,Whole genome sequences,"Between 2015 and 2021, human immunodeficiency virus type 1 (HIV-1) whole genome sequencing was performed on samples from people with recently acquired HIV-1 in the United Kingdom. The complete genomic sequencing of HIV was performed using a previously described sequence capture method and the short read data were assembled into consensus whole genomes using Genomancer, an in-house viral genome assembly pipeline",The paper mentions that 'human immunodeficiency virus type 1 (HIV-1) whole genome sequencing was performed.' This indicates that the whole genome of the virus was sequenced.
41004608,5,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,United Kingdom,"Between 2015 and 2021, human immunodeficiency virus type 1 (HIV-1) whole genome sequencing was performed on samples from people with recently acquired HIV-1 in the United Kingdom. The UKHSA has sequenced HIV whole genomes from all individuals identified to have recently acquired HIV-1 in the UK since 2015 as part of routine HIV surveillance.",The paper specifies that the samples were obtained from people with recently acquired HIV-1 in the United Kingdom.
41004608,6,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,2015 to 2021,"A total of 1182 people had available WGS data between 2015 and 2021. The UKHSA has sequenced HIV whole genomes from all individuals identified to have recently acquired HIV-1 in the UK since 2015 as part of routine HIV surveillance. Between 2015 and 2021, human immunodeficiency virus type 1 (HIV-1) whole genome sequencing was performed on samples from people with recently acquired HIV-1 in the United Kingdom. Of 1106 participants, 375 (34%) started an INSTI-based regimen. Of these, 337 (90%) were men and 196 (52%) were living with subtype B. The median age was 33 years and number of viral loads within 24 months of starting ART was 4.",The paper mentions that whole genome sequencing was performed on samples from people with recently acquired HIV-1 between 2015 and 2021.
41004608,7,What method was used for sequencing?,Whole genome sequencing,"The complete genomic sequencing of HIV was performed using a previously described sequence capture method and the short read data were assembled into consensus whole genomes using Genomancer, an in-house viral genome assembly pipeline",The paper describes the use of whole genome sequencing to obtain the sequences of HIV from patient samples.
41004608,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,No,"The complete genomic sequencing of HIV was performed using a previously described sequence capture method and the short read data were assembled into consensus whole genomes using Genomancer, an in-house viral genome assembly pipeline",The paper does not mention any cloning of samples prior to sequencing. It describes the use of a sequence capture method and short read data assembly.
41004608,9,What type of samples were sequenced?,Clinical specimens,"The UKHSA has sequenced HIV whole genomes from all individuals identified to have recently acquired HIV-1 in the UK since 2015 as part of routine HIV surveillance. All samples with sufficient leftover volume that have undergone avidity testing for recency of acquisition were eligible for WGS. Recent acquisition, defined as being in the preceding 6 months, is determined by the recent infection testing algorithm (RITA), which uses the results of an HIV-1 antibody avidity assay and clinical characteristics. RITA excludes those with evidence of treatment at time of sampling, and so the sequences to which WGS was applied were strictly pretreatment.","The paper mentions that the samples were from individuals identified to have recently acquired HIV-1, and they had undergone avidity testing for recency of acquisition."
41004608,10,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,No,"The UKHSA has sequenced HIV whole genomes from all individuals identified to have recently acquired HIV-1 in the UK since 2015 as part of routine HIV surveillance. All samples with sufficient leftover volume that have undergone avidity testing for recency of acquisition were eligible for WGS. Recent acquisition, defined as being in the preceding 6 months, is determined by the recent infection testing algorithm (RITA), which uses the results of an HIV-1 antibody avidity assay and clinical characteristics. RITA excludes those with evidence of treatment at time of sampling, and so the sequences to which WGS was applied were strictly pretreatment. RITA results were available for approximately  21% of those newly diagnosed during 2015–2021.","The paper mentions sequences were pretreatment, no individual with virological failure."
41004608,11,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,No,"Between 2015 and 2021, human immunodeficiency virus type 1 (HIV-1) whole genome sequencing was performed on samples from people with recently acquired HIV-1 in the United Kingdom. All individuals with available UKHSA WGS data, and linked clinical metadata from the UK's HIV and AIDS Reporting System (HARS), were eligible for inclusion. The UKHSA has sequenced HIV whole genomes from all individuals identified to have recently acquired HIV-1 in the UK since 2015 as part of routine HIV surveillance. All samples with sufficient leftover volume that have undergone avidity testing for recency of acquisition were eligible for WGS.",The paper does not mention that the patients were part of a clinical trial. It describes the sequencing of samples as part of routine HIV surveillance.
41004608,12,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,1182,"A total of 1182 people had available WGS data between 2015 and 2021. Of these, 76 HIV acquisitions could not be confirmed to be recent (Figure 1).",The paper states that 'A total of 1182 people had available WGS data between 2015 and 2021.' This indicates the number of individuals from whom samples were obtained for sequencing.
41004608,13,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,No,"All samples with sufficient leftover volume that have undergone avidity testing for recency of acquisition were eligible for WGS. Recent acquisition, defined as being in the preceding 6 months, is determined by the recent infection testing algorithm (RITA), which uses the results of an HIV-1 antibody avidity assay and clinical characteristics. RITA excludes those with evidence of treatment at time of sampling, and so the sequences to which WGS was applied were strictly pretreatment.","The paper mentions sequences were pretreatment, with enough left samples in individuals."
41004608,14,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,Not reported,"The complete genomic sequencing of HIV was performed using a previously described sequence capture method and the short read data were assembled into consensus whole genomes using Genomancer, an in-house viral genome assembly pipeline. All samples with sufficient leftover volume that have undergone avidity testing for recency of acquisition were eligible for WGS. Recent acquisition, defined as being in the preceding 6 months, is determined by the recent infection testing algorithm (RITA), which uses the results of an HIV-1 antibody avidity assay and clinical characteristics. RITA excludes those with evidence of treatment at time of sampling, and so the sequences to which WGS was applied were strictly pretreatment.",The paper does not provide information on the drug classes received by individuals before sequencing. It focuses on  sequences from individuals identified to have recently acquired HIV-1.
41004608,15,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,Not reported,"The complete genomic sequencing of HIV was performed using a previously described sequence capture method and the short read data were assembled into consensus whole genomes using Genomancer, an in-house viral genome assembly pipeline. All samples with sufficient leftover volume that have undergone avidity testing for recency of acquisition were eligible for WGS. Recent acquisition, defined as being in the preceding 6 months, is determined by the recent infection testing algorithm (RITA), which uses the results of an HIV-1 antibody avidity assay and clinical characteristics. RITA excludes those with evidence of treatment at time of sampling, and so the sequences to which WGS was applied were strictly pretreatment.",The paper does not provide specific information on the drugs received by individuals before sequencing. It focuses on  sequences from individuals identified to have recently acquired HIV-1.
41004608,16,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,No,"No GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates were provided in the text of the paper. The presence of clinically relevant drug resistance mutations (surveillance drug resistance mutations [SDRMs]) was identified by submitting sequences to the Stanford Calibrated Population Resistance tool [15]. This tool both identifies established SDRMs and applies sequence and mutation-level exclusion criteria to remove potentially spurious findings based on factors including low coverage, multiple APOBEC mutations, or adjacency to insertions, deletions, or frame shifts",The paper does not mention that the sequences were made publicly available. It focuses on the analysis of mutations and their prevalence.
