41056006,10,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,Yes,"Emergence of LEN resistance was an exploratory endpoint. HIV-1 capsid genotypic and phenotypic data were assessed at study entry using the GenoSure Gag-Pro and PhenoSense Gag-Pro assays (Monogram Biosciences). Resistance testing was performed for any participants who met one of the following virologic failure criteria: suboptimal virological response, defined as two consecutive visits with HIV-1 RNA ≥50 copies/mL and a decline of <1log10 from Day 1 to Week 10; virological rebound, defined as two consecutive visits with HIV-1 RNA ≥50 copies/mL after reaching <50 copies/mL, or two consecutive visits with an increase from nadir of >1log10; or participants with HIV-1 RNA ≥50 copies/mL at last study visit.",The paper mentions that resistance testing was performed for participants who met virologic failure criteria.
41056006,11,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,Yes,"Design. CALIBRATE was a Phase 2, randomized, open-label study (NCT04143594).",The paper describes a clinical trial (CALIBRATE) in which the participants were enrolled.
41056006,12,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,<= 10,"Resistance testing was performed for any participants who met one of the following virologic failure criteria: suboptimal virological response, defined as two consecutive visits with HIV-1 RNA ≥50 copies/mL and a decline of <1log10 from Day 1 to Week 10; virological rebound, defined as two consecutive visits with HIV-1 RNA ≥50 copies/mL after reaching <50 copies/mL, or two consecutive visits with an increase from nadir of >1log10; or participants with HIV-1 RNA ≥50 copies/mL at last study visit.","The paper states that resistance testing was performed for a select group of participants, indicating that specific sequences were not reported."
41056006,13,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,Yes,"Design. CALIBRATE was a Phase 2, randomized, open-label study (NCT04143594). Treatment-naive PWH were randomized (2:2:2:1) to four treatment groups (TG): TG1 and TG2 received twice-yearly subcutaneous lenacapavir plus oral daily emtricitabine/tenofovir alafenamide (F/TAF); TG3 received oral daily lenacapavir plus F/TAF; and TG4 received oral daily bictegravir/F/TAF. At W28, TG1 switched to lenacapavir plus TAF and TG2 switched to lenacapavir plus bictegravir. At W80, TG4 completed the study and TG1-3 continued assigned treatments.",The paper involves treatment-naive individuals who received one of three treatment regimens.
41056006,14,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"NRTIs, INSTIs","Treatment-naive PWH were randomized (2:2:2:1) to four treatment groups (TG): TG1 and TG2 received twice-yearly subcutaneous lenacapavir plus oral daily emtricitabine/tenofovir alafenamide (F/TAF); TG3 received oral daily lenacapavir plus F/TAF; and TG4 received oral daily bictegravir/F/TAF. At W28, TG1 switched to lenacapavir plus TAF and TG2 switched to lenacapavir plus bictegravir. At W80, TG4 completed the study and TG1-3 continued assigned treatments.",The treatment regimens included drugs from the nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor (NRTI) and integrase strand transfer inhibitor (INSTI) classes.
41056006,15,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"Lenacapavir, Emtricitabine, Tenofovir alafenamide, Bictegravir","Treatment-naive PWH were randomized (2:2:2:1) to four treatment groups (TG): TG1 and TG2 received twice-yearly subcutaneous lenacapavir plus oral daily emtricitabine/tenofovir alafenamide (F/TAF); TG3 received oral daily lenacapavir plus F/TAF; and TG4 received oral daily bictegravir/F/TAF. At W28, TG1 switched to lenacapavir plus TAF and TG2 switched to lenacapavir plus bictegravir. At W80, TG4 completed the study and TG1-3 continued assigned treatments.","The treatment regimens included lenacapavir, emtricitabine, tenofovir alafenamide, and bictegravir."
41056006,16,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,No,"Data availability statement. Gilead Sciences shares anonymized individual participant data upon request or as required by law or regulation with qualified external researchers based on submitted curriculum vitae and reflecting non-conflict of interest. The request proposal must also include a statistician. Approval of such requests is at Gilead Science's discretion and is dependent on the nature of the request, the merit of the research proposed, the availability of the data, and the intended use of the data. Data requests should be sent to datarequest@gilead.com.","The paper did not provide any GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced isolates, and the data are available upon request."
