41130593,5,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,South Africa,The LEN resistance-associated mutation K70R was also detected in one South African participant with a subtype C virus and no exposure to LEN.,"The paper mentions a participant from South Africa with a subtype C virus, indicating that samples were obtained from this country."
41130593,6,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,2021 to 2023,"The remaining 11 participants who acquired HIV-1 after Day 1 (4 participants in P1 and 7 in P2) were evaluated for resistance, “August 2021–September 2023”",The paper mentions the study duration from August 2021 to September 2023.
41130593,7,What method was used for sequencing?,Next-generation sequencing,"Genotypic CA resistance testing at Monogram was conducted using a next-generation sequencing platform (MiSeq; Illumina), with reporting of mutants present in   	c10% of sequences obtained for a given sample.",The paper describes the use of a next-generation sequencing platform (MiSeq; Illumina) for genotypic resistance testing.
41130593,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,No,No evidence mentions the cloning of samples prior to sequencing.,The paper does not mention any process of cloning samples prior to sequencing.
41130593,9,What type of samples were sequenced?,Plasma,"Upon HIV-1 diagnosis, plasma samples were collected for HIV-1 RNA quantification and resistance analyses.",The paper states that plasma samples were collected for HIV-1 RNA quantification and resistance analyses upon HIV-1 diagnosis.
41130593,10,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,Yes,The LEN resistance-associated mutation K70R was also detected in one South African participant with a subtype C virus and no exposure to LEN. This is likely a rare polymorphism.,"The paper mentions the detection of resistance mutations, which indicates sequences were obtained from individuals with virological failure."
41130593,11,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,Yes,"The PURPOSE trials assessed the efficacy of LEN and emtricitabine/tenofovir disoproxil fumarate (F/TDF) in cisgender women (PURPOSE 1; P1) and in cisgender men, transgender women, transgender men and gender nonbinary persons (PURPOSE 2; P2).","The paper describes the PURPOSE trials, indicating that the patients were part of a clinical trial."
41130593,12,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,53,Resistance to LEN was detected in 0 of 2134 participants (P1) and 2 of 2179 participants (P2); both developed N74D. Four participants in each study receiving LEN were,"Resistance to LEN was detected in 0 of 2134 participants (P1) and 2 of 2179 participants (P2); both developed N74D. Four participants in each study receiving LEN were untouched or unexplained HIV-1 discovery at recruitement4. In P1, 2/37 participants needle for resistance in the F/TAF group possessed M184I ± K65R. In the F/TDF groups, M184M/I/V was detected in 1/16 participants (P1) and 1/9 participants (P2). Resistant bacteria to LEN was detected in 0 of 2134 participants (P1) and 2 of 2179 participants (P2); both developed N74D. So total individuals for resistance testing are 53."
41130593,13,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,Yes,"In the F/TAF group, 2 participants had wild type (WT) HIV-1 CA and acquired HIV-1 between Day 1 and Week 26. Upon HIV-1 diagnosis, genotypic analysis was performed for resistance. In P1, 2/37 participants analyzed for resistance in the F/TAF group had M184I ± K65R. In the F/TDF groups, M184M/I/V was detected in 1/16 participants (P1) and 1/9 participants (P2).","The paper mentions participants received study drugs at Day 1 but were later found to have acquired HIV-1 before study initiation, and participants receiving F/TAF or F/TDF total  P1  2 / 37  participants  F / TAF  group and  1 / 16  1 /09  participantsin  FTDF  group so sequences obtained from individuals who had received ARV drugs."
41130593,14,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"NRTIs, NNRTIs.","PURPOSE 1 and PURPOSE 2 included participants receiving F/TDF or F/TAF for preexposure prophylaxis, participants in F/TAF group possessed M184I  ␀c±K65R, in F/TDF group, M184M/I/V detected; non-study drug resistance mutations detected in 20 of 60 P1 participants tested for resistance. No resistance mutations detected in 60 of 60 P2 participants tested for resistance.","The paper mentions participants in F/TAF or F/TDF group, M184M/I/V was detected which indicates NRTIs were received, also M184M was detected which indicates NNRTI was received."
41130593,15,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"Emtricitabine, Tenofovir Alafenamide, Tenofovir Disoproxil Fumarate","The PURPOSE trials assessed the efficacy of LEN and emtricitabine/tenofovir disoproxil fumarate (F/TDF) in cisgender women (PURPOSE 1; P1) and in cisgender men, transgender women, transgender men and gender nonbinary persons (PURPOSE 2; P2).",The paper mentions the participants received emtricitabine/tenofovir disoproxil fumarate (F/TDF) or emtricitabine/tenofovir alafenamide (F/TAF) for preexposure prophylaxis.
41130593,16,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,No,No evidence mentions that sequences from the paper were made publicly available.,The paper does not mention any publicly available sequences from the study.
41140464,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,No,"2.1. Study Overview. This study employed a meta-analysis approach to evaluate the subtype distribution, diversity and drug resistance of the HIV-1 pol gene across EA. Data on HIV-1 pol gene sequences were retrieved from public database. Using appertaining software, the sequences were analyzed for assessment of DRMs in the pol gene enzymes (PR, RT, and IN).","The paper mentions that the study employed a meta-analysis approach to evaluate the subtype distribution, diversity, and drug resistance of the HIV-1 pol gene across East Africa. It states that data on HIV-1 pol gene sequences were retrieved from public databases, and not obtained from patient samples directly, hence no sequences were reported from patient samples."
41140464,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,No,"We retrieved 7614 HIV-1 pol gene sequences, deposited between 2015 and 2025 from the Los Alamos HIV databases.",The paper focuses on genetic diversity and drug resistance patterns of HIV-1 pol gene sequences obtained from public databases. It does not mention performing in vitro drug susceptibility tests.
41140464,3,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,Not reported,No evidence,The paper does not provide any specific GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates. It mentions data retrieval from public databases but does not list accession numbers.
41140464,4,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,"PR, RT, IN","Using appertaining software, the sequences were analyzed for assessment of DRMs in the pol gene enzymes (PR, RT, and IN).","The paper mentions the assessment of DRMs in the pol gene enzymes, specifically mentioning the regions of PR (Protease), RT (Reverse Transcriptase), and IN (Integrase) that were analyzed."
41140464,5,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,"Kenya, Uganda, Tanzania, Ethiopia","The sequences were sourced from four EA countries: Kenya, Uganda, Tanzania, and Ethiopia. Table 1: The HIV-1 pol gene sequence from East Africa retrieved from public database by June 2025.","The paper lists the countries from which the HIV-1 pol gene sequences were retrieved, specifically mentioning Kenya, Uganda, Tanzania, and Ethiopia."
41140464,6,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,2015-2025,"We retrieved 7614 HIV-1 pol gene sequences, deposited between 2015 and 2025 from the Los Alamos HIV databases. In June 2025, HIV-1 pol gene sequences deposited between 2015 and 2025 from four East African countries were retrieved in FASTA format with subtyping information from the Los Alamos National Laboratory (LANL) HIV Database",The paper mentions that the data on HIV-1 pol gene sequences were retrieved from public databases for sequences deposited between 2015 and 2025.
41140464,7,What method was used for sequencing?,Not reported,No evidence,The paper does not specify the exact sequencing method used for the HIV-1 pol gene sequences. It focuses on the analysis of sequences retrieved from databases.
