40431742,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,Yes,"Samples from 1667 PLWHA were analyzed: 81.2% were male, with 52.6% identifying as men who have sex with men. A total of 1677 genotypes from PLWHA classified as ART-naive were recorded. The demographic, clinical, and immuno-virological profiles are detailed in Table 1.","The paper describes the analysis of HIV-1 sequences from patient samples, specifically mentioning that samples from 1667 PLWHA were analyzed for resistance mutations."
40431742,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,Yes,"Results: Samples from 1667 PLWHA were analyzed: 81.2% were male, with 52.6% identifying as men who have sex with men. According to the WHO list, the overall TDR was 12.1% (n = 203). The prevalence of RAMs was 10.1% (170/1667) for NNRTIs, 4% (67/1667) for nucleoside reverse-transcriptase inhibitors (NRTIs), and 1.7% (30/1667) for protease inhibitors (PIs). The most frequent NNRTI mutations were K103N (5.6%), G190A (0.89%), and K103S (0.77%). The prevalence of DOR RAMs was <2%, with the most common being Y188L (0.53%). Rilpivirine RAM prevalence was 6%. Susceptibility to DOR, RPV, efavirenz, and nevirapine as given by the Stanford algorithm was 97.4%, 92%, 91.4%, and 90.4%, respectively. The ANRS criteria yielded susceptibility rates of 98.3%, 93.3%, 92.3%, and 90.8%, respectively. Regarding NRTIs, thymidine analog mutations (including T215 revertants) were the most frequent RAMs. Among PIs, the most prevalent RAMs were M46L (0.47%) and V82A (0.35%). Conclusions: Our study shows the persistence of moderate to high levels of resistance to first-generation NNRTIs. Despite this, prevalence was low for DOR. Surveillance of TDR remains critical for recommendations of ART initiation.","The paper includes data on the predicted susceptibility of different drugs based on the resistance mutations found, indicating in vitro drug susceptibility assessment."
40431742,3,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,No,No evidence,The paper does not mention any GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates.
40431742,4,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,"PR, RT","Briefly, HIV-1 resistance genotyping was used for the identification of RAMs in the HIV-1 polymerase (pol) gene. The final PCR product was 1084 base pairs in length, encompassing the protease and reverse-transcriptase regions of the HIV-1 pol gene.","The paper mentions that the study involved sequencing the HIV-1 pol gene, which includes the protease (PR) and reverse transcriptase (RT) regions."
40431742,5,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,Argentina,"This study analyzed genotype results gathered from plasma samples drawn as part of routine clinical practice from naïve adult PLWHA from two reference HIV-clinics in Buenos Aires, Argentina.","The samples were obtained from two reference HIV clinics in Buenos Aires, Argentina, as part of a cross-sectional study."
40431742,6,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,2017-2021,"The study was a retrospective cross-sectional, non-interventional study, conducted over the period 2017-09/2021.",The samples were collected between 2017 and 2021 as stated in the study design.
40431742,7,What method was used for sequencing?,Sanger sequencing,"The sequencing products were analyzed on an Applied Biosystems/Hitachi 3500 Genetic Analyzer (Waltham, MA, USA).","The paper describes the use of the Applied Biosystems/Hitachi 3500 Genetic Analyzer, which is consistent with Sanger sequencing technology."
40431742,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,No,The paper does not mention any cloning of samples prior to sequencing.,The study did not mention any cloning of samples before sequencing.
40431742,9,What type of samples were sequenced?,Plasma,"All plasma samples were processed and stored for the determination of drug resistance mutations at the Laboratorio Dr. Stamboulian molecular biology division in Buenos Aires, Argentina, according to standardized procedures.",The paper specifies that plasma samples were used for the genotyping and resistance mutation analysis.
40431742,10,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,No,"This study analyzed genotype results gathered from plasma samples drawn as part of routine clinical practice from naïve adult PLWHA from two reference HIV-clinics in Buenos Aires, Argentina, ensuring systematic testing of all collected samples. Participants aged 18 years or older, at the time of genotype sampling. Documented HIV-1 infection (based on a reactive Enzyme-Linked Immunosorbent Assay plus Western blot or detectable viral load). Treatment-naive, defined as no antiretrovirals (in combination or monotherapy) received before resistance test based on clinical records.","The paper focused on treatment-naive participants, indicating that none of the individuals had experienced virological failure on a treatment regimen."
40431742,11,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,No,"This study analyzed genotype results gathered from plasma samples drawn as part of routine clinical practice from naïve adult PLWHA from two reference HIV-clinics in Buenos Aires, Argentina, ensuring systematic testing of all collected samples. PLWHA participating in clinical trials for HIV treatment or prevention.",The paper explicitly states that participants were not involved in clinical trials for HIV treatment or prevention.
40431742,12,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,1667,"Samples from 1667 PLWHA were analyzed: 81.2% were male, with 52.6% identifying as men who have sex with men.",The paper states that samples from 1667 PLWHA were analyzed for resistance mutations.
40431742,13,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,No,"This study analyzed genotype results gathered from plasma samples drawn as part of routine clinical practice from naïve adult PLWHA from two reference HIV-clinics in Buenos Aires, Argentina, ensuring systematic testing of all collected samples. Participants aged 18 years or older, at the time of genotype sampling. Documented HIV-1 infection (based on a reactive Enzyme-Linked Immunosorbent Assay plus Western blot or detectable viral load). Treatment-naive, defined as no antiretrovirals (in combination or monotherapy) received before resistance test based on clinical records.","The paper focused on treatment-naive participants, indicating that none of the individuals had received ARV drugs before the samples were obtained."
40431742,14,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,None,"This study analyzed genotype results gathered from plasma samples drawn as part of routine clinical practice from naïve adult PLWHA from two reference HIV-clinics in Buenos Aires, Argentina, ensuring systematic testing of all collected samples. Participants aged 18 years or older, at the time of genotype sampling. Documented HIV-1 infection (based on a reactive Enzyme-Linked Immunosorbent Assay plus Western blot or detectable viral load). Treatment-naive, defined as no antiretrovirals (in combination or monotherapy) received before resistance test based on clinical records.","The paper specifies that the study focused on treatment-naive participants, meaning they received no ARV drugs prior to sample sequencing."
40431742,15,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,None,"This study analyzed genotype results gathered from plasma samples drawn as part of routine clinical practice from naïve adult PLWHA from two reference HIV-clinics in Buenos Aires, Argentina, ensuring systematic testing of all collected samples. Participants aged 18 years or older, at the time of genotype sampling. Documented HIV-1 infection (based on a reactive Enzyme-Linked Immunosorbent Assay plus Western blot or detectable viral load). Treatment-naive, defined as no antiretrovirals (in combination or monotherapy) received before resistance test based on clinical records.",The paper focuses on treatment-naive individuals who had not received any ARV drugs before the sample was obtained.
